  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Beirut Electric Mobility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progoris / WAVE Bike started its pilot for an e-bike subscription plan in Beirut, Lebanon to solve part of its traffic problem. During this pilot phase WAVE has tested 15 bikes in the local environment and has tested its supply chain. The pilot attracted external financing to purchase 75 new bikes to arrive in December 2020. Sustainability and safety are key components, as the app linked to the project has been fully integrated with the bikes and provides its users safe routings throughout the city. To ensure circularity, the company is also testing if the batteries will be re-usable in solar energy panels. The pilot, made with DGGF-TA, has led to 12 direct jobs, of which 6 female and 6 youth. 6 indirect jobs were funded and 11 people were trained on maintenance of the bikes, marketing, management and the training of future staff.</narrative>
  </description>
